 input\ninput: {\n    "question": "<p><a href=\\"http://jsfiddle.net/KrA3D/\\" rel=\\"nofollow\\">http://jsfiddle.net/KrA3D/</a></p>\\n\\n<p>I tried to run this both locally and in the jsfiddle without success. Am I missing something? I want to make this image move to the right.</p>\\n\\n<p>HTML</p>\\n\\n<pre><code>&lt;div id=\\"game\\"&gt;\\n    &lt;img id=\\"asd\\" src=\\"http://i.imgur.com/ApuSWMC.png\\" alt=\\"torch\\"&gt;\\n&lt;/div&gt;\\n</code></pre>\\n\\n<p>JS</p>\\n\\n<pre><code>$(document).ready(function () {\\n    $(\'#asd\').click(function () {\\n\\n        $(\'#asd\').animate({\\n            left: \\"+=100px\\"\\n        }, \'fast\');\\n\\n    });\\n\\n}); \\n</code></pre>\\n\\n<p>I thought it has to do with the selector, tried both by <code>id</code> and <code>img</code>, tried changing it to a <code>div</code>, without success. Any idea what might be wrong?</p>",\n    "answer": "I\'m afraid there\'s no way to animate CSS properties directly. You have to use JavaScript to change the value of the property over time. Here\'s an example:\\n\\n```\\n<div id=\\"asd\\"></div>\\n<script>\\nvar div = document.getElementById(\'asd\');\\nsetInterval(function(){\\n    div.style.left = parseInt(div.style.left || 0) + 10 + \'px\';\\n}, 10);\\n</script>\\n<style>\\n#asd{\\n    position:absolute;\\n    width:100px;\\n    height:100px;\\n    background:red;\\n}\\n</style>\\n```"\n}\nOutput: ', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct', 'n': 1, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.01}}
